From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Let the host say how big a surface is on this console.

With 0880 the composition swapchain reaches Vulkan, and the screen goes
black -- the title hands the display over the moment a Vulkan surface is
created ("display released to vulkan close=state shown=0"). Then:

    thunk32_vkCreateSwapchainKHR 0xba1c88, 0x21fa38, 0, 0x21f9f8
    fixme:dxgi:hresult_from_vk_result Unhandled VkResult -3.

VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED, and the whole stack tears itself down:
swapchain, surface, images, memory. Nothing paints, and nothing can,
because the title's own video output is already closed.

adjust_surface_capabilities overwrites the host's image extents with the
window's client rect, so that an application sees what the Win32 WSI would
have told it. That is right where a window system exists. Here there is
none: ps5drv answers every vulkan_surface_create with a headless surface
whatever HWND it is handed, and RADV's WSI scans that out through
sceVideoOutRegisterBuffers, which registers buffers of the video mode's
size and of no other size. So the client rect is a fiction, the extents
are not, and telling vkd3d to ask for a swapchain the size of the window
dxgi invented in 0880 asks the scanout for something it cannot make.

Leave the host's extents alone under __PROSPERO__. The maxImageCount fix
above it stays: that one is about what applications expect, not about what
the window system can do.

Two more things, because a refusal here is otherwise a bare number:

  - vkCreateSwapchainKHR raised the requested extent to the host's minimum
    and never lowered it to the host's maximum, so an oversized request was
    refused rather than clamped. Clamp both ways.

  - On failure, log the request and the capabilities it was built from.
    RADV's own stderr goes nowhere from inside a PRX, so these eleven
    fields are the only evidence there is about which one it objected to.
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
index 7fadce04de..cddf9eaf41 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -1602,6 +1602,25 @@ static void adjust_surface_capabilities( struct vulkan_instance *instance, struc
      */
     if (!capabilities->maxImageCount) capabilities->maxImageCount = max( capabilities->minImageCount, 16 );
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ The window is a fiction on this console and the host's extents are not.
+     * Every surface here is the display: ps5drv answers vulkan_surface_create
+     * with a headless surface whatever HWND it is handed, and RADV's WSI scans
+     * that out through sceVideoOutRegisterBuffers, which registers buffers of
+     * the video mode's size and of no other size. Overwriting the host's
+     * extents with a client rect therefore tells the application to ask for a
+     * swapchain the scanout cannot make, and RADV refuses it with
+     * VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED and no message on any channel we receive.
+     *
+     * GTA IV reached exactly that: a composition swapchain at the size of the
+     * window dxgi invented for it, vkCreateSwapchainKHR -> -3, and a black
+     * screen, because by then the title had already handed the display over to
+     * Vulkan and nothing else was ever going to paint it.
+     *
+     * The maxImageCount fix above stays -- it is about what applications
+     * expect, not about what the window system can do. */
+    (void)client_rect;
+#else
     /* Update the image extents to match what the Win32 WSI would provide. */
     /* FIXME: handle DPI scaling, somehow */
     get_surface_rect( surface->hwnd, &client_rect, get_dpi_for_window( surface->hwnd ) );
@@ -1611,6 +1630,7 @@ static void adjust_surface_capabilities( struct vulkan_instance *instance, struc
     capabilities->maxImageExtent.height = client_rect.bottom - client_rect.top;
     capabilities->currentExtent.width = client_rect.right - client_rect.left;
     capabilities->currentExtent.height = client_rect.bottom - client_rect.top;
+#endif
 }
 
 static VkResult win32u_vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfaceCapabilitiesKHR( VkPhysicalDevice client_physical_device, VkSurfaceKHR client_surface,
@@ -1851,6 +1871,14 @@ static VkResult win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR( VkDevice client_device, const VkSwa
 
     create_info_host.imageExtent.width = max( create_info_host.imageExtent.width, capabilities.minImageExtent.width );
     create_info_host.imageExtent.height = max( create_info_host.imageExtent.height, capabilities.minImageExtent.height );
+    /* ⚠ And back down again. The extent was only ever raised to the host's
+     * minimum; a caller that asks for more than the host's maximum -- which on
+     * this console is the video mode, the one size the scanout has buffers for
+     * -- gets its swapchain refused rather than clamped. */
+    if (capabilities.maxImageExtent.width)
+        create_info_host.imageExtent.width = min( create_info_host.imageExtent.width, capabilities.maxImageExtent.width );
+    if (capabilities.maxImageExtent.height)
+        create_info_host.imageExtent.height = min( create_info_host.imageExtent.height, capabilities.maxImageExtent.height );
 
     /* If the swapchain image size is not equal to the presentation size (e.g. because of DPI virtualization or
      * display mode change emulation), MoltenVK's vkQueuePresentKHR returns VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR.
@@ -1871,6 +1899,27 @@ static VkResult win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR( VkDevice client_device, const VkSwa
 
     if ((res = device->p_vkCreateSwapchainKHR( device->host.device, &create_info_host, NULL, &host_swapchain )))
     {
+        /* ⚠ Say what was asked for. A host WSI that refuses a swapchain here
+         * reports nothing through any channel this console delivers -- RADV's
+         * own stderr goes nowhere from inside a PRX -- so the request and the
+         * capabilities it was built from are the only evidence there is, and
+         * without them a refusal is a bare number with eleven fields behind
+         * it. */
+        ERR( "vkCreateSwapchainKHR failed, res %d: format %u, colorSpace %u, extent %ux%u, images %u, "
+             "layers %u, usage %#x, sharing %u, preTransform %#x, compositeAlpha %#x, presentMode %u, "
+             "clipped %u, old %p\n", res, create_info_host.imageFormat, create_info_host.imageColorSpace,
+             create_info_host.imageExtent.width, create_info_host.imageExtent.height,
+             create_info_host.minImageCount, create_info_host.imageArrayLayers, create_info_host.imageUsage,
+             create_info_host.imageSharingMode, create_info_host.preTransform, create_info_host.compositeAlpha,
+             create_info_host.presentMode, create_info_host.clipped,
+             (void *)(UINT_PTR)create_info_host.oldSwapchain );
+        ERR( "host capabilities: images %u..%u, extent %ux%u (%ux%u..%ux%u), layers %u, transforms %#x, "
+             "alpha %#x, usage %#x\n", capabilities.minImageCount, capabilities.maxImageCount,
+             capabilities.currentExtent.width, capabilities.currentExtent.height,
+             capabilities.minImageExtent.width, capabilities.minImageExtent.height,
+             capabilities.maxImageExtent.width, capabilities.maxImageExtent.height,
+             capabilities.maxImageArrayLayers, capabilities.supportedTransforms,
+             capabilities.supportedCompositeAlpha, capabilities.supportedUsageFlags );
         free( swapchain );
         return res;
     }
